<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $23.86 bln on Nov 22.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $23.86 bln on Nov 22.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.94 billion on November 22, 1996, from $23.86 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Nov 22	Nov 15	 Nov 24</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,532	19,427	 17,561</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,382	 4,382	  4,408</p>
<p>    SDRs				    26	    51	     18</p>
<p>    Total			     23,940	23,860	 21,987</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
